<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">stat-edge</ansi>

Stats grow smoothly with each level (<ansi fg="command">help progression</ansi>). So in a
fight, the <ansi fg="yellow">difference</ansi> between your stat and your opponent's is what counts,
point by point, never the ratio of the two.

Each opposed chance has a value at equal stats. Every point you are ahead
moves it 1/{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} of the way to its best value; every point behind, 1/{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} of the way to its worst. A lead of {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} points reaches the bound.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Hit</ansi>          Speed against Speed: {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitEven" }}% even, {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitMin" }}% to {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitMax" }}%.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Critical</ansi>     Smarts against Smarts: {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.CritChanceEven" }}% even, {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.CritChanceMin" }}% to {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.CritChanceMax" }}%.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Tackle</ansi>       Speed against Perception: 40% even, 20% to 80%.

Some chances only grow when you are ahead, starting from their minimum:
dodge and critical damage (Perception), parry (Speed), shield bash and the
Strength part of your damage bonus (Strength). A block moves either way
with Strength.

For example, with Speed 4 against a foe's 3, you hit 1/{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} of the way
from {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitEven" }}% toward {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.ToHitMax" }}%.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help speed</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help smarts</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help perception</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strength</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help defense</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
